# HARNESS-ONLY / non-normative: the reference reads the size of a scene's canvas from the canvas object, but the
# size of canvas-less scenes (and of groups without canvas) from the main video mix. A real core keeps both equal;
# the fake core can desynchronise them with canvas_mix_only. An implementation with a single "main canvas size"
# does not need to reproduce this script.
source cam 100 100
scene m
scene n none
add m cam i1
add n cam i3
pos i1 960 540
pos i3 960 540
canvas_mix_only 800 600
get i1
get i3
